---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show the usage hours of recent runs, newest first.

Columns: RUN ID, HOURS, STARTED, ENDED. STARTED and ENDED are the start and end
of the billable usage of the run, in the local timezone.

With --rollup, each row is the total of one day, week, or month, in the local
timezone. A week starts on Monday. Columns: DATE, RUNS, HOURS. DATE is the last
day of the period. A period with no runs does not show. When --started-after or
--started-before cuts a period, the total of that period includes only the runs
inside the filter.

--started-after and --started-before filter on the time that the usage of a run
started. --limit counts rows: runs, or periods with --rollup.

Examples:
  snouty runs usage
  snouty runs usage --rollup week -n 4
  snouty runs usage --rollup month --started-after 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each row prints as one JSON object on
its own line. A run has the fields run_id, hours, start_time, and end_time; the
times are RFC 3339 in the local timezone. A period has the fields date, runs,
and hours:
  snouty --json runs usage --rollup month | jq -r '"\(.date) \(.hours)"'

Usage: snouty runs usage [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --rollup <ROLLUP>
          Total the runs of each day, week, or month, in the local timezone
          
          [possible values: day, week, month]

      --started-after <STARTED_AFTER>
          Only show runs started after this timestamp (ISO 8601)

      --started-before <STARTED_BEFORE>
          Only show runs started before this timestamp (ISO 8601)

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of rows to display: runs, or periods with --rollup
          
          [default: 10]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
